{"title":"Career roadmap — Credit Analyst","role":"Credit Analyst","summary":"A Credit Analyst evaluates the creditworthiness of individuals, businesses, or institutions to determine whether financing should be approved and on what terms. The role combines accounting, financial statement analysis, credit risk, banking, data analysis, and financial judgement.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Com (Bachelor of Commerce)","Course":"B.Com – Accounting & Finance"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Com graduate, the strongest route is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Accounting","Financial Analysis","Credit Assessment","Banking Products","Risk Management","Credit Analytics","Advanced Credit Risk"]}]},{"heading":"Career horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","What to focus on"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Accounting, financial statements, Excel, financial ratios, banking fundamentals, credit appraisal"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"Corporate credit, risk modelling, portfolio analysis, SQL/Power BI, sector analysis"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"Credit risk analytics, automation, AI/ML, portfolio risk, stress testing"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"AI-driven underwriting, real-time credit decisions, alternative data, advanced risk strategy"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Accounting & finance foundation"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Financial accounting"},{"text":"Cost accounting"},{"text":"Corporate finance basics"},{"text":"Balance Sheet"},{"text":"Profit & Loss Statement"},{"text":"Cash Flow Statement"},{"text":"Working capital"},{"text":"Revenue and expenses"},{"text":"Assets and liabilities"},{"text":"Depreciation"},{"text":"Inventory"},{"text":"Receivables and payables"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Learn Excel:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":